= Campaigning

The party needs support from many people in China to enstate itself as the true government. How should we campaign among our demographics?

- @rural: Rural workers and small farmers, the largest demographic in China.
- @workers: The working class, labourers in the cities.
- @new_middle: The "new middle class" of students, intellectuals and white-collar workers.
- @old_middle: The "old middle class" of traditional independent businessmen and artisans.
- @unemployed: The unemployed.
- @root: We either don't want to or cannot campaign right now.
- @easy_discard

@workers
subtitle: -1 funds
choose-if: funds >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough funds.
on-arrival: workers_kmt += 4*(1-dissent); workers_kmt -= 2 if unemployed >= 15; workers_kmt -= 3 if unemployed >= 25; funds -= 1;

We have increased our support among the workers. [? if unemployed >= 15: The high levels of unemployment make our campaign more difficult. ?]

@new_middle
subtitle: -1 funds
choose-if: funds >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough funds.
on-arrival: new_middle_kmt += 4*(1-dissent); funds -= 1;

We have increased our support among the new middle class.

@old_middle
subtitle: -1 funds
choose-if: funds >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough funds.
on-arrival: old_middle_kmt += 4*(1-dissent); funds -= 1;

We have increased our support among the old middle class.

@rural
subtitle: -1 funds
choose-if: funds >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough funds.
on-arrival: rural_spd += 5*(1-dissent); funds -= 1;

We have increased our campaigning among farmers. [? if peoples_party == 0: We have not historically campaigned much among the farmers, and they do not trust us. ?][? if peoples_party > 0: As a people's party, we have an easier time increasing support among farmers than before. ?][? if rural_policy >= 2 : Our rural policies have made it easier for us to build support among farmers. ?]

@unemployed
subtitle: -1 funds
choose-if: funds >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough funds.
on-arrival: unemployed_spd += 3*(1-dissent); funds -= 1;

We have increased our campaigning among the unemployed.

@root
subtitle: No campaigning, for now.
go-to: main
